[COMMENTS]
STATION,Crump profile weir gauging a Chalk catchment with predominantly arable land use and significant artificial deposits. GENERAL: Crump profile weir, 2.5m broad (wing wall height 1.6m), situated immediately upstream of road bridge. Prior to 1973 thin-plate weir, 1.45m broad. Also called Gutter Bridge. STATION HYDROMETRY: Current theoretical rating fits well to gaugings. Two ratings applied across period of record, the most recent is valid from December-1973 when crump weir installed necessitating a change in rating. Part of the Lodes-Granta groundwater support scheme, operated according to site conditions. FLOW RECORD: Data between 26-03-2017 to 09-04-2017 marked as suspect; tree branches were found to be blocking the weir. Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in October 2018 (WINFAP Files v7) and August 2025 (WINFAP Files v14). FLOW REGIME: Regime influenced by groundwater abstraction/recharge. Significant groundwater abstractions for public water supply. Runoff increased by effluent returns.
CATCHMENT,Chalk with no appreciable superficial deposits. Predominantly arable land use. Catchment boundary manually digitised due to issue with IHDTM incorrectly delineating the upper catchment.
Qmed Suitability,Gauged above QMED. Flow remains modular with good fit to gaugings.
Pooling Suitability,Weir expected to drown at approximately 0.33m which is not accounted for in current rating.
[END]
